{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/962236-mysterium-can-t-lie","id":962236,"title":"Mysterium can't lie?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-02T06:52:03-07:00","id":962236,"title":"Mysterium can't lie?","content":"Mysterium has their own, lower rules - called Protocols - and one of which is that they cannot lie to others. ( See <b>Mysterium</b> Order book for this. ) So is this mean the do not lie to mages only? They can cheat Sleepers all the time? Because I got this answer when mentioning subject in other topic...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/961192-problem-\u2013-nameless-mage-in-pentacle-cabal?p=961655#post961655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The mysterium protocol is to not lie to other mages about magic knowledge directly. They can lie as much as they want to sleepers, and they can lie to other mages but when a mage ask them &quot;does X magic thingie exist&quot; and its classified and/or dont feel like answering they can say &quot;i cant confirm or deny that&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T06:56:33-07:00","id":962240,"title":"","content":"At work, so I can't check books, but LokiRavenSpeak has the gist of it. The Protocols are against spreading the Lie, not lies in general, even if I recall the book mentioned a specific, radical party within the Mysterium who doesn't see the difference between the two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T07:10:13-07:00","id":962248,"title":"","content":"They can't lie about <i>magic</i>. Some of them choose not to lie about anything, but that's not Mysterium doctrine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T07:11:24-07:00","id":962249,"title":"","content":"Mysterium Pg. 57 doesn't mention if Mystagogues are allowed to lie to Sleepers or not but the protocol seems to pertain entirely to mystical knowledge. Members can lie by omission, give incomplete mundane information, or simply refuse to answer a question. If they impart any actually magical knowledge though they must give the information in its entirety.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T07:15:02-07:00","id":962252,"title":"","content":"From what I remember, it was not lying about magic. They could lie about anything from parking tickets to breaking consilium law, but lying about a certain tome or artefact's capabilities is not okay.<br /> <br /> That said, I don't go with the &quot;I can neither confirm or deny&quot; approach for very many. My favorite is the flat out &quot;I can't tell you&quot; or the slightly more fun &quot;I'll look into it&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Wow I wish I had something cool to say here</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2227-dman1123","name":"dman1123","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T07:54:48-07:00","id":962281,"title":"","content":"They believe that Magic is a Living Thing made up from Living Symbols. When you successfully lie, you invoke a symbol of thing opposite to the living symbol that magic is made up from, thus making Lie stronger. Basically, they are afraid that each time you lie about magic, somewhere A Magic Kitten Symbol dies. It's different from saying &quot;It's classified&quot; - because that's not lying! - but saying &quot;Yeah, sure, this thing here doesn't exist, go away&quot; means that you punched Magic in the face and helped Exarchs curbstomp it.<br /> <br /> This is why, by the way, some members of Mysterium might have reputation of being dicks; while someone else would tell you a white lie, their religious belief forces them to tell you &quot;I don't want you to know&quot; or &quot;I think you shouldn't know this&quot; instead of &quot;No, I don't know about this&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T10:38:24-07:00","id":962362,"title":"","content":"Something important to note is where this belief comes from: Pancryptia. Mystagogues believe in the magical equivalent of a signal to noise ratio; that Truth can be hidden behind a Lie; that light can be concealed under a bushel. Mystagogues don't like to lie because covering up the Truth actively weakens the Supernal and wounds the Living Mysteries. In instances where Pancryptia is not an issue (such as a lie that will be shown to be false in short order or which might otherwise be corrected soon), it may be permissible to lie, but those situations would be rare. In most peaceful interactions with a fellow Mage, it's unacceptable.<br /> <br /> It's noted in the books that Sleepers don't usually count for this, though I'm not entirely sure why. It might just be the traditional anti-Sleeper bigotry mystagogues tend to be carrying around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T11:09:13-07:00","id":962378,"title":"","content":"Well it's that and the fact that Sleepers who were given factually correct magical information might induce Dissonance on the topic. Or so the theory goes anyway. Mysterium point to the increasing rarity of ruins from Before as a possible example of this, Sleeper walks onto magical site, and then proceeds to erode all the magic out of it by accident. As a result it's just easier to not tell them the truth about any of it or risk a negative confirmation by saying they won't talk about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T20:09:58-07:00","id":962656,"title":"","content":"It's like being a scientist. If you're writing a study to be published or you get on the news and says &quot;We've discovered X&quot;, then it's completely inappropriate to lie or falsify your results. Not everyone's that honest, but they do risk their professional credibility if they get caught. The Mysterium takes this idea of keeping knowledge pure even more seriously because it's also a religious belief for a lot of them.<br /> <br /> However when that same scientist at home says to his daughter, &quot;If you're not ready in ten minutes we're leaving without you and you won't get to go to Disneyland.&quot; That might be a lie, but it's not going to corrupt scientific knowledge. Likewise Mages can lie to one another about all sorts of trivial, non-magical things without contributing to Pancryptia.<br /> <br /> The Mysterium has no policy on talking to sleepers about magic, because it's redundant. Talking to sleepers about magic violates the Lex Magica.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T11:18:06-07:00","id":964413,"title":"","content":"As i was quoted on this thread i almost missed<br /> <br /> About what they can and cant lie about the book is pretty clear<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mysterium;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A true magus never lies to her colleagues about the nature and properties of secret knowledge. She may refuse to speak about a subject in whole or part, but must never mislead one of the Awakened.</div> </div> </div> </div>So yes, a mysterium mage can lie and say to the hierarch that his decision wasnt stupid or that he totally is respect by everyone etc etc<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/962236-mysterium-can-t-lie?p=962249#post962249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mysterium Pg. 57 doesn't mention if Mystagogues are allowed to lie to Sleepers or not but the protocol seems to pertain entirely to mystical knowledge. Members can lie by omission, give incomplete mundane information, or simply refuse to answer a question. If they impart any actually magical knowledge though they must give the information in its entirety.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is incorrect, on the pages 57 at the end of the &quot;thou shall not lie&quot; protocol.<br /> <br /> Right of scholarship<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mysterium;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">None of these obligations apply to Sleepers or other supernatural beings. Mages don\u2019t owe them any honesty at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 09-06-2016, 02:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T11:41:25-07:00","id":977865,"title":"","content":"Real tough case my player brought up - What about Mysteries and Obsessions? Like, if other mage ask Mysterium member 'Did you saw vampires/werewolves/Prometheans/etc?' what can they answer to him? They surly can say &quot;I can't tell you&quot;, bt what about lying on this? Or maybe 'I did see' but lying on details?<br /> <br /> Mysteries are not direct Supernal Lore, don't they?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T11:59:45-07:00","id":977873,"title":"","content":"Mysteries are magical the Mysterium doesn't care if the magic is from the Supernal, they don't lie about magic. Just look at the quotes from the book by LRS in the post right above yours, &quot;...never lies to her colleagues about the nature and properties of secret knowledge...&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T18:02:27-07:00","id":978086,"title":"","content":"It's just about magic and magic-related topics. If someone asks for information about a sinister artifact to help them find it and you don't think they're worthy enough or capable enough to use that information safely, a mystagogue should say &quot;I am not going to give you any help&quot; instead of lying about it to aim them in the wrong direction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When one is accustomed to privilege, equality seems like oppression.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7195-tidygamer","name":"TidyGamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7195_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"644"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}